atlas optimization-preservation-boundary

architecture preservation-boundary
  canonical_name PreservationBoundary
  owns PreservationLayer
  owns DualStatus
  owns SemanticLineage
  consumes ProductContract
  consumes CapabilityBinding
  consumes CascadePlan
  publishes DualStatus
  publishes PromotionVerdict
  family optimization
  domain Optimization / Protected boundary
  layer governance
  semantic_question Which layer is this change allowed to alter, and does the layer above it still mean exactly what it meant before?
  purpose Draw the line the optimization doctrine may not cross. Bonfyre may compress representation, execution, cognition, context and repeated structure. It may not compress away business semantics, user-visible capability, authority, or the legacy behavior being preserved.
  maturity architectural
  node_types PreservationLayer
  node_types ProtectedSemantics
  node_types OptimizableRealization
  node_types DualStatus
  node_types SemanticLineage
  edge_types preserved_by
  edge_types realized_by
  edge_types factored_beneath
  invariant three layers exist and only the lowest may change aggressively
  invariant the product-semantics layer is what the client bought and uses; it is never a compression target
  invariant the exact-compiled layer must remain exactly equivalent to the product layer, not approximately equivalent
  invariant a binding retains enough semantic lineage to reconstruct the original behavior; its physical representation may be tiny, its meaning may not be tiny by omission
  invariant repetition in legacy code is evidence of shared mechanics, never evidence that behavior is disposable
  invariant scheduled and background behavior is product capability; invisibility on a screen is not absence
  invariant a downstream user sees named domain sections, never capability identifiers; the packed representation stays under the floorboards
  invariant factoring makes behavior more discoverable; a factoring that reduces the census of what exists has erased rather than compressed
  forbidden_inference a route looking repetitive -> its business behavior being disposable
  forbidden_inference two routes sharing mechanics -> those routes being one capability
  forbidden_inference a capability having no screen -> that capability not existing
  forbidden_inference a faster implementation -> an equivalent implementation
  forbidden_inference a shared kernel -> merged business domains
  forbidden_inference legacy behavior being strange -> that behavior being unintentional
  interacts compression-law
  interacts optimization-cascade
  interacts optimization-proof
  interacts product-contracts
  source_lineage Generation-10 optimization doctrine promotion, 2026-08-26
  source_lineage downstream product chain preservation ruling, 2026-08-26

layer l1-product-semantics
  rank 1
  mutability protected
  detail What users actually bought and use. Transfer a horse, submit a daysheet, generate a statement, apply a payment, run vet production, schedule a transfer, change a billing cycle, download a report, request a correction.
  invariant never a compression target

layer l2-exact-compiled
  rank 2
  mutability equivalence-bound
  detail Address, capability binding, product contract, business rules, effects, authority, schedules, evidence and proof. Provides exact equivalence between the layer above and the layer below.
  invariant equivalence here is exact, never statistical

layer l3-optimized-realization
  rank 3
  mutability aggressive
  detail Content identity and dedup, packed identifiers and bitsets, columnar and adjacency forms, deltas, byte compression, borrowed views, latent reduction, cheap cognition routing, prepared context and model state, residency, fused and lowered kernels.
  invariant free to change entirely, provided layer 2 equivalence holds

dual_status semantic_preservation
  values PASS, FAIL
  question Does it still mean, read, calculate, change, emit and prove exactly what it did?
dual_status physical_optimization
  values PASS, FAIL
  question Is it admissibly represented under the optimization gates?

verdict semantic_PASS_physical_PASS
  outcome promotable
verdict semantic_PASS_physical_FAIL
  outcome correct but still fat; keep optimizing; not a defect in behavior
verdict semantic_FAIL_physical_PASS
  outcome reject; a fast wrong answer is the worst outcome the doctrine can produce
verdict semantic_FAIL_physical_FAIL
  outcome reject

lineage_field legacy_route
lineage_field domain_subject
lineage_field domain_action
lineage_field input_contract
lineage_field filter_contract
lineage_field business_rules
lineage_field calculation_family
lineage_field read_closure
lineage_field write_closure
lineage_field effect_class
lineage_field authority_contract
lineage_field external_systems
lineage_field scheduled_trigger
lineage_field output_contract
lineage_field report_or_document_contract
lineage_field evidence_contract
lineage_field regression_contract
lineage_field current_implementation
lineage_field alternate_realizations
lineage_field exact_legacy_provenance

acceptance_rule preserve
  detail what it means, who uses it, what it reads, what it calculates, what it changes, what it emits, when it runs, and what proves it worked
acceptance_rule factor
  detail repeated route wrappers, repeated validation shapes, repeated report mechanics, repeated permissions, repeated relationships, repeated allocation mechanics, repeated workflow structure
acceptance_rule optimize
  detail identity, storage, memory, copying, queries, search, cognition, context, models, scheduling, physical execution
acceptance_rule lower
  detail only after repeated proof, and only with a demonstrated lift or thaw path

archaeology_role
  detail Cheap cognition may propose where business logic hides in a legacy tree: whether a unit belongs to a domain family, is validation, is authorization, is formatting only, is a dead wrapper, is a shared helper, is a domain calculation or is a scheduled workflow.
  bounded_by cheap-cognition
  invariant it tells the exact machinery where to dig; it never declares what was found

interaction preservation-bounds-cascade
  source preservation-boundary
  destination optimization-cascade
  relation hard_constraint
  preserves the product-semantics layer and the exact-equivalence obligation of the compiled layer
  drops any optimization that reduces the census of what behavior exists
  forbidden_inference a cascade stage being admissible in general -> that stage being admissible across a preservation layer
  witness none

interaction preservation-reports-dual-status
  source preservation-boundary
  destination optimization-proof
  relation verdict_input
  preserves the separation of semantic preservation from physical optimization as two independent statuses
  drops any single combined score that would let a semantic failure be offset by a physical success
  forbidden_inference a fast implementation -> a preserved implementation
